 This package enables ESC testing with a turtlebot with a rotating sensor frame. This package includes several ROS2 nodes built specifically to work with the sensors and servo motors used in the vehicle construction. Please use the turtlebot launch file to configure and start and experiment. This package is intended to be used with ros_esc, ros_esc_interfaces, and extremum-seeking packages from the DSIM Lab Gitlab.
 
+## Phase 09 selected GESC plus Gaussian profile
+
+The selected physical workflow uses the existing launch and node owners with
+the cumulative Phase 08 runtime through v8.12. The new
+`gesc_gaussian_two_source_voltage.bash` wrapper defaults to the primary
+scenario, reads the stable serial device from reviewed calibration, builds the
+three reviewed physical ROS packages, sources the resulting workspace, and
+runs the launch inside the sole `ros_esc record_run` readiness/recording owner.
+Use `--scenario secondary` only for the separately reviewed secondary layout.
+
+The managed run prints its unique output directory and a one-second diagnostic
+summary in the same terminal. Its sqlite3 rosbag retains every legacy physical
+sensor/filter/control/odometry stream plus the typed GESC/Gaussian diagnostics;
+the run directory also contains logs, completeness evidence, resolved ROS
+state, and hashed copies of the exact reviewed input files.
+
+Keep commissioned copies of the calibration and scenario metadata under
+`~/.config/dsim-lab/phase09/`; the checked-in/installed copies remain inert
+templates and rebuilds never become the owner of site measurements. The first
+commissioning run is `--stationary-preflight`: calibration and every readiness
+flag remain false, the passive timekeeper replaces the servo/GPIO owner, and
+both base and rotating-sensor actuation are forbidden. It requires the typed
+`PREFLIGHT <operator> | <observer>` confirmation and a live serial/Vicon data
+plane, then runs for a fixed 15 seconds. Review its retained offline PASS before
+using `--approve-stationary RUN_DIRECTORY --reviewer NAME` on the site metadata
+copy. Neither action authorizes motion or calibration.
+
+Later rotating-photoresistor calibration must retain a sqlite3 rosbag directory,
+an exact resolved-configuration mapping, and a structured calculation output.
+The calculation output has `schema_version: 1`, the independently computed raw
+bag and resolved-configuration SHA-256 values, and exact `measurements` and
+`analysis` mappings copied from the reviewed calibration document. The validator
+rehashes all three artifacts and cross-checks protocol, firmware, stable serial
+identity, rotation counts, median/MAD intervals, negative-voltage sign/range,
+source responses, and metadata before motion readiness can pass.
+
+A bounded configuration-only audit performs no serial, Vicon, ROS graph, or
+command access:
+
+```bash
+bash "$(ros2 pkg prefix --share turtlebot3_vehicle_nodes)/bash_scripts/light_esc_experiments/voltage_cost_values/gesc_gaussian_two_source_voltage.bash" --check-only
+```
+
+After commissioning has passed, the primary run is intentionally one entry
+point with no required arguments:
+
+```bash
+bash "$(ros2 pkg prefix --share turtlebot3_vehicle_nodes)/bash_scripts/light_esc_experiments/voltage_cost_values/gesc_gaussian_two_source_voltage.bash"
+```
+
+The real run requires an interactive `RUN <operator> | <observer>` confirmation
+covering the clear floor, independent stop, and ready Vicon server. There is no
+noninteractive bypass. The wrapper creates a temporary run-specific metadata
+copy and retains it together with the immutable commissioned template.
+
+Use `--scenario secondary` for the second selected layout. `Ctrl+C` requests a
+managed stop, final zero, bag finalization, completeness validation, and scoped
+cleanup.
+
+The checked-in Phase 09 calibration is intentionally uncalibrated and blocks
+the wrapper. Do not mark it motion-ready from simulator values. Live Pi
+transfer, the no-actuation stationary preflight, emergency-stop/nontranslating
+rehearsal, rotating-photoresistor calibration, and motion each retain their
+separate authorization and review gates.
+
+The selected robust graph uses wheel/IMU-backed `/odom` for every algorithm
+pose input, monitors `/imu`, and keeps exactly one `/cmd_vel` publisher. A new
+Phase-09-only Vicon node publishes required ground truth as
+`geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped` on
+`/gesc_gaussian/evaluation/vicon_pose`. Vicon loss blocks/revokes evidence
+readiness, but Vicon values, evaluator coordinates, and lamp roles never enter
+control. Historical Vicon/odometry code and the legacy CSV collector remain
+unchanged and selectable only through their existing experiment paths. The
+operator ends a managed run with `Ctrl+C`, which lets readiness fall false,
+records final zero commands, finalizes the bag, and performs scoped cleanup.
+
